     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Reading kanji in words",
     "texto": [
      "Kanji are used inside words to write names and meaningful parts. The same kanji can have different readings depending on the word: learn **the whole word with its reading**, not one universal reading of the character.",
      "In verbs and adjectives, kanji are usually accompanied by hiragana: 食べます (たべます), 大きい (おおきい). Particles continue in hiragana: 日本人 **は** 学生 **です**."
